WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.930
English puts its little
words after the verb:

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.380
I gave it to him.

3
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.650
French piles them up in front:

4
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.390
«Je le lui ai donné.» There,

5
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.980
it comes before him.

6
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.960
But a friend lends you something:

7
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.490
«Elle me le prête.» Now it comes second.

8
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.540
And sometimes even more
tiny words join the queue:

9
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.560
«Il y en a trois.» Three sentences,

10
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.410
three different line-ups.

11
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.710
So who decides which tiny word goes first?

12
00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.330
In this mission, you'll
stand at a two-way sign

13
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.680
and choose a road for each pronoun.

14
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.950
Then you'll find out
where the queue stops when

15
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.990
a sentence has two verbs.

16
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: crack the code that
decides which tiny word goes first.
